        "link": "https://aclanthology.org/2021.emnlp-main.627/",
        "snippet": "Transformer-based architectures have become the de-facto standard models for a wide range of Natural Language Processing tasks. However, their memory footprint and high latency are prohibitive for efficient deployment and inference on resource-limited devices. In this work, we explore quantization for transformers. We show that transformers have unique quantization challenges–namely, high dynamic activation ranges that are difficult to represent with a low bit fixed-point format. We establish that these activations contain …",
